Changelog: 12-11-2026 14:51:59

Release 3.1.0.

Changelog: 12-11-2026 14:22:00

Fixed. The Settings tab no longer opens with a line of explanation above its boxes (owner, 12-11-2026: no long lines of
text in the window); the boxes start at the top. What the line said is in the wiki chapter's Settings section.

Changelog: 12-11-2026 14:00:06

Added. The Game folder line names the folders alone, and what goes in them is behind an info symbol beside it (owner,
12-11-2026: as shadPS4 Manager's; no long lines of text in the window): "Drop your games in ~/Games/XBOX360, .ISO,
unpacked discs, .zar archives, Games on Demand and Arcade packages. A USB drive or an SD card with a Games/XBOX360
folder is also checked for content." The wiki chapter's Game folder line says so.

Changelog: 12-11-2026 13:24:27

Added. A tab Start game (owner, 12-11-2026: in the game apps a tab that starts the selected game in Steam): the last
tab is a button (core's ActionTab). A click starts the game chosen under Your games through Steam, as its shortcut
there does: the shortcut's number is read from Steam's file (core's steam.shortcut_number) and steam://rungameid/ is
opened for it, so Steam starts first when it does not run. The tab that was open stays open, and the keyboard passes
the tab by. Without a chosen game, or with one that is not in Steam yet, the line under the tabs says what to do first
and nothing starts. The wiki chapter has a Start game section; "The app has no Play button" is gone from it.

Changelog: 12-11-2026 13:24:26

Added. Escape closes the window, as its close button does, and so does B on a controller (owner, 12-11-2026: inside
the apps the B button and the Escape key exit the app, as they exit the portal): an open menu first, then a question
or a dialog, then the window. A key the window takes for itself comes first, and a window that is busy still asks
before it closes. B is read with pygame-ce from the suite's venv, only while the app has the focus and has had it for
half a second, so the press that closed another app does not close this one too; without pygame-ce or a controller
there is Escape alone. __main__ calls core's exit_keys's install().

