Changelog: 10-11-2026 02:13:33

Release 3.0.1.

Changelog: 10-11-2026 00:27:26

Fixed. install.sh makes the shared Python venv again when an older Python made it. After a Bazzite update moves
/usr/bin/python3 to a new version, the venv no longer finds its packages (PyQt6, pip): the app did not start, and
running install.sh again stopped at pip.

Changelog: 10-11-2026 00:19:00

Release 3.0.0.

Changelog: 07-11-2026 20:18:45

Breaking. The window is built as RPCS3 Manager's (owner, 07-11-2026: RPCS3 Manager's design is every manager's). The app
has no Play button any more: a game is started from Steam, and a double-click on a game no longer starts it. Settings…
is gone: Xenia's settings are in the Settings tab. Covers… is now Steam artwork…, Update Game Mode is now Update Steam,
the Game Mode column is In Steam and the In Game Mode box is Available in Steam. The messages box under the table is
gone: what the app says is in the Log tab.

Changelog: 07-11-2026 20:18:45

Added. The header has the Refresh pill and the boxes, Xenia version, Your games and Available in Steam, spread over the
window's width, with the app's state beside the title. Under the introduction, which links to Xenia's release notes and
to the wiki, stands a row of action pills: Xenia Install and Xenia Uninstall, a third of the width each. The state of
each follows in two lines, then three tabs: Your games (the table with Xenia settings, Remove game…, Steam artwork… and
Update Steam, and a link that opens Steam's library), Settings and Log. What the app says and does goes to its log,
~/.local/share/bc250-xenia-manager/bc250-xenia-manager.log (turned over at 1 MB), shown in the Log tab; install.sh
--uninstall keeps it, --purge removes it. The tabs, the pills and the choice boxes take RPCS3 Manager's style.

Changelog: 07-11-2026 20:18:45

Added. The Xenia line under the pills says only the state, in the words every manager uses (owner, 07-11-2026): "Not
installed." with "Install it with the Install button." under it, or "Installed." with "Uninstall with the Uninstall
button." under it. The version installed, what Install takes, another version than the app brings, and a newer Xenia are
in the line's tooltip; another version and a newer Xenia also go to the log, once.

